  clock: 2  # c1a6
  nonce: c1a6  # c1a6
  message: "PER-FILE NARROWING, checked 2026-11-14 at the owner's request (evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/per_file_narrowing_check_11142026). THE RULE: a file that blocks keeps everything selected for it (its import slice, the tests the index saw executing it, the declarative additions); only a test selected solely for files that do not block may be dropped, by the existing test. SOUNDNESS: it adds no assumption. A dropped test is one the selector would not run if the blocking files were changed alone, and one narrowing would drop if the other files were changed alone; ADR-0010 already composes the prose-only rule per file the same way. WHAT IT GIVES UP: in a mixed change today, the tests selected for the other files also run against the blocking file's change. That is the only cover for a test that depends on a blocking file without importing it (analyzers loaded through the registry); how many such tests exist was not measured. MEASURED: of the 88 PRs since 10-30 that changed package source, 17 have no blocking file, 48 have only blocking files, 23 are mixed. On the 23, estimated with today's import graph and the 11-12 index, slice only: the rule would drop 1,126 of 11,312 selected test files, median 3 per PR, max 246, nothing on 7. On PR #2183 it would drop 0 of 1,032 (base.py blocks and nearly every test imports it). PREREQUISITE: the index currently loses true edges (filed today as an invariant), so no rule that narrows more often is safe until that is fixed. This rule and the statement-level rule of this item are complementary: this one needs no judgement about which statements are safe."  # c1a6
- op: discuss  # 40b4
  at: '2026-11-14T21:39:23Z'  # 40b4
  by: agent  # 40b4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 40b4
  clock: 3  # 40b4
  nonce: 40b4  # 40b4
  message: "MEASUREMENT AND BED SOUNDNESS, 2026-11-14 (evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/falas_measure_11142026; nothing implemented, the ruling belongs to the owner). METHOD: every changed import-time block diffed statement by statement against its base (nested defs elided as the digest does), each added, removed or modified statement given a kind; files that are prose-only are left out because smart-test takes them out before narrowing. PER COMMIT (last 400 on dev): 98 modify coverable package source, 70 refused today; admitted by (i) 2, by (ii) 4, by (i)+(ii) 8. PER PR (last 150 manifest commits, 10-30 to 11-14): 90 change package source, 71 refused today (79 percent); admitted by (i) 1, by (i)+(ii) 3. WHAT BLOCKS THE 71 (PRs showing each kind): module docstring text changed in a file whose code also changed 42; computed assignment value changed 28; from-import gained a name 22; import of a module not imported before 17; new literal constant with a fresh private name 16, public name 9; new computed assignment 12; literal constant value changed 10; new class attribute 10; new frozenset or tuple call of literals to a fresh private name 9; new re.compile of literals 4. TWO FURTHER CANDIDATES THE DATA SUGGESTS: (iv) a module or class docstring edit in a file whose code also changed, keeping the tests the prose record shows reading that file, its docstrings or line numbers: (i)+(ii)+(iv) admits 10 of 71; (v) a new assignment of frozenset, tuple, set, dict, list or re.compile of literals to a fresh name: with it 14 of 71. CANDIDATE (iii) IS ALREADY IN EFFECT: a new method or property is a new block and never refuses, with no base or subclass check; in the change that prompted this item the FileIndex refusal came from the __slots__ assignment. That path is unsound and is filed separately (INV-bifih, override of an inherited method). SAVING (run set is the manifest each PR committed; index of 11-12; the INV-tabal complete-run condition taken as met; test seconds are per-test means summed, not wall): (i)+(ii) 3 PRs, 557 of 1,667 selected test files dropped, 765 of 8,760 test seconds; with (iv) 10 PRs, 1,700 of 4,013 files, 4,050 of 22,510 s; with (v) 14 PRs, 2,477 of 5,479 files, 6,218 of 31,531 s. All 90 source-changing PRs selected 42,291 test files and 232,518 test seconds, so the three sets save 0.3, 1.7 and 2.7 percent of the test seconds of the window. BED (prototype in worktree ~/hg_wt/falas, patch in prototype/; 16 new edits, text oracle for the admitted kinds): on a module nothing enumerates, each of literal private, literal public, from-import name and container call narrows and drops 0 MUST; the mixed docstring edit drops 0 MUST with the prose-record keep and drops the test that reads the module docstring at runtime without it; all 8 unsafe kinds (new module import, computed assignment, rebinding, builtin name, class attribute, from-import of a submodule, __all__, constant value change) are still refused with every candidate admitted (narrowing drops nothing). UNSOUND CASE FOUND: on a module whose namespace a test pins with dir(), (i) with a public name, (i) with a private name and (ii) each drop that test, which fails on the edit (3 of 3). A test is exposed when it enumerates the module (itself, or through a function of another module such as catalog.py line 202, vars(module)) and has coverage rows elsewhere and none in the changed file. 17 files under the test and script roots use dir(), vars(), getmembers(), __dict__ or a star import. A test file with any test that leaves no coverage row is never dropped, which shields a test that only enumerates. NOT DONE: no count of real tests in the exposed position; (iv) and (v) were not in the item and have no soundness argument beyond the bed rows above; the 11-12 index stands in for the index of each PR day. RECOMMENDATION (mine): do not build (i)+(ii): 3 of 71 refused PRs and 0.3 percent of test seconds, against a namespace-enumeration hole that needs its own guard. If one candidate is built, (iv) is the largest (7 more PRs) and rests on evidence the prose-only rule already records. A separate selector defect found on the way outranks all of this: the slice leaves out tests that reach a changed module through the import of another module (INV-mikag, P2)."  # 40b4
